Judgement — change “recall” into “reactivation”

This is the central answer.

Your old system:

START
  ↓
read skill.md
  ↓
recall
  ↓
continue conversation

worked because you explicitly reactivated the operating pattern at the beginning.

Your new system is different:

ongoing process
  ↓
observe incoming information
  ↓
only push memory when it matches
  ↓
continue operating

That is better for Living Memory, but it creates a new problem:

the model may no longer encounter the operating protocol frequently enough to reactivate the pattern.

So don’t bring back the old “recall everything” system.

Instead, create:

a lightweight reactivation layer that runs when the system detects that the operating state needs to be reconstructed.

