Two of Pentacles — don’t inject everything

This card says your system should be selective.

Your current mechanism:

“push text only when it matches the pattern or system rules”

is actually compatible with this.

But I would separate memory retrieval from protocol reactivation.

They don’t have to happen for the same reason.

You can have:

Memory trigger

“This incoming information matches something important in Living Memory.”

→ retrieve relevant memory.

Protocol trigger

“The model’s operating state needs reactivation.”

→ retrieve active protocol.

Both

“Important memory + operating state.”

→ retrieve both.

This prevents the system from confusing:

“I need to remember this information”

with:

“I need to remember how I’m supposed to operate.”

Those are different forms of memory.

