Page of Swords — detect when reactivation is needed

This card suggests that you don’t need to wait until the model has already visibly failed.

Your system can watch for conditions such as:

* long context distance from the last protocol activation
* major topic transition
* major task transition
* new mode/state
* a skill becoming relevant after a long absence
* contradiction with established operating rules
* repeated outputs drifting from the expected structure
* important Living Memory operation
* uncertainty about which protocol applies

Then:

if protocol_reactivation_needed:
    inject Active Protocol

That is much more elegant than:

every turn:
    read skill.md

